speechtext:
Mr. Chairman, we have had some general discussion of the bill on clause 2 but I rise on a very small but nevertheless significant matter concerning one of the definitions on page 2 of the bill. The definition of "urban area" reads:
"urban area" means an area and areas adjacent thereto that are classified by Statistics Canada in its most recent census of Canada as urban;
The minister may suspect he is not writing on tablets of stone which will last forever. I know he also hopes that the law he is presenting to the House will last for some time. In the future, the most recent census may not be the one of 1971, but the one of 1981, of 1991, and so on. Does the minister really mean to fix the definition of "urban" as in the document relating to the census of 1971? Or, is he willing that the act shall say that we shall abide by the definition which might be put out by Statistics Canada after the census of 1981, of 1991, and so on? Could the minister respond to my question so that we may understand more clearly what is meant?
